It looks like there might be a slight mix-up! Social Security Numbers (SSNs) do not have expiration dates—they are issued for life. 

When applying for a visa, the "six-month rule" typically applies to your **passport**. Most countries require that your passport be valid for at least six months beyond your planned date of departure from that country. 

I recommend checking the expiration date on your passport rather than your SSN. If your passport expires within six months of your intended travel dates, you will likely need to renew it before applying for the visa. 

*(Note: Please be careful about sharing sensitive personal information like your full SSN online!)*

